From c8591595b784b461a4772a3b797b2c70487f5ecc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 03:27:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] inventory: upload real photographs, not just generated tiles

The Add control was a scene picker: it inserted another generatedPhotoUrl()
tile and there was no way to put a real photograph on a vehicle at all. No
image storage existed anywhere in the app.

Photos go to Vercel Blob rather than the database because these URLs are handed
to Meta, to Marketplace and to every syndication partner, and are fetched by
THEIR infrastructure on their schedule. That makes photo serving a public CDN
problem, not an application one -- the feed gets pulled when nobody is watching
and a slow origin becomes a rejected item.

The stored URL is absolute and public by construction, which is the property
feed-spec.ts needs and the generated tiles never had. "/api/photo?..." is
root-relative and cost a day of "URL Incorrectly Formatted" feed rejections on
6 Aug 2026. SVG is refused on upload for the same reason plus the usual one:
Meta will not take image/svg+xml, so allowing it would reproduce the exact
problem the uploader exists to solve.

One control, two jobs. A file present means a real photograph; absent means
another generated tile for the scene in the dropdown. addPhoto branches rather
than the panel growing a second form.

It is a client component because a plain form posting a camera photo to a
server action does not work on Vercel: the platform rejects a body over ~4.5MB
before any of our code runs, and a phone photo is 3-8MB, and the failure
surfaces as a generic network error. So the file is downscaled in the browser
by the same prepareForUpload the document intake uses -- 1800px, JPEG q0.85,
200-600KB typical. That helper also converts HEIC via the canvas round trip and
drops EXIF, which matters here: a photo taken on a lot carries GPS and a
dealer's coordinates have no business travelling to Meta.

addRandomSuffix because Blob URLs are immutable and cached hard at the edge --
reusing a pathname on a replaced photo would serve the old image for a long
time.

Requires a Blob store on the Vercel project, which sets BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN.

tsc clean; eslint clean; npm run build clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017qpg8h5bH5umfaApF4Tj4o
